# FILE: .gitattributes
# ROLE: Normalises line endings to LF everywhere and marks binary artefacts.
# ARCH REF: FR-4; D-36
# OWNS: Line-ending and binary rules
# DOES NOT OWN: Ignore rules (.gitignore)
# CONNECTS TO (external boundaries only):
#   - imports from none: none
#   - emits/consumes: none
# INSTRUCTIONS (strict, imperative):
#   1. Implement only this file. If this file's contract with another file must change, stop and report; do not edit the other file.
#   2. Keep `* text=auto eol=lf`; add new binary extensions below rather than per-file rules.
# FORBIDDEN: CRLF-specific rules; per-OS exceptions
# ERRORS: A wrong rule shows up as whole-file diffs after checkout on Windows.
# DONE WHEN: (1) `git ls-files --eol` shows lf for all text files on Windows and Linux. (2) `uv run python scripts/check_headers.py` reports no problem for this file.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.gguf binary
*.safetensors binary
*.bin binary
*.pt binary
*.onnx binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.db binary
*.sqlite binary
*.zip binary
